CI/CD — What’s Actually Happening Behind the Scenes?

> When I first heard about CI/CD, I honestly thought it was just some fancy automation buzzword.

But after playing around with Jenkins and GitHub, I finally get it.

Here’s what really happens when you push your code 👇

🧩 Continuous Integration (CI):
Every time you commit code, Jenkins (or GitHub Actions) jumps in  builds your project, runs tests, and checks if you accidentally broke something. Basically, your friendly robot tester 🤖

🚀 Continuous Deployment (CD):
Once everything passes, it automatically sends your updated code straight to the server (like AWS EC2 or Kubernetes). No manual steps. No “works on my machine” drama.

In short:
CI/CD = Code goes from laptop → production → live — automatically.

That’s the real DevOps magic ✨
